    "1. Replace the single unsided LazyOptional field with a per-side cache (Map<Direction, LazyOptional<?>>) or, for a simpler two-sided case, two LazyOptional fields (e.g. frontHandler / backHandler).",
    "2. In getCapability(cap, side): guard on cap == ForgeCapabilities.ITEM_HANDLER AND !this.remove (or this.isAlive() for entities). Return the per-side LazyOptional, creating it lazily via a factory that inspects the current BlockState and the requested side to build the correct IItemHandler (e.g. SidedInvWrapper, a custom handler, or InvWrapper for the default side).",
    "3. Override setBlockState(BlockState): before calling super, invalidate every cached per-side LazyOptional (set field to null, call old.invalidate()). This mirrors the ChestBlockEntity patch pattern and prevents a stale handler from surviving a state change.",
    "4. Override invalidateCaps(): call super.invalidateCaps(), then invalidate all per-side LazyOptionals (iterate the map or null-out each field).",
    "5. Override reviveCaps(): call super.reviveCaps(), then clear the per-side cache (set fields to null or clear the map) so the next getCapability call re-creates handlers from the fresh state.",
    "6. In the per-side factory method, validate that the BE is still attached to a valid level and that the block state is still the expected type before constructing the handler; fall back to an empty/InvWrapper handler otherwise.",
    "7. Ensure the handler itself does not hold a hard reference to a Container that may be replaced (e.g. double-chest Container) without triggering invalidation; if the Container can change, invalidate the cache when it does."
  ],
  "code_or_pseudocode": "public class MyBlockEntity extends BaseContainerBlockEntity {

    // Per-side cache instead of a single unsided field
    private LazyOptional<IItemHandler> frontHandler;   // e.g. Direction.NORTH
    private LazyOptional<IItemHandler> backHandler;    // e.g. Direction.SOUTH
    private LazyOptional<IItemHandler> defaultHandler; // all other sides

    // --- Lifecycle: state change ---
    @Override
    public void setBlockState(BlockState newState) {
        super.setBlockState(newState);
        // Invalidate all cached handlers so they are rebuilt from the new state
        invalidateSideHandler(frontHandler);  frontHandler = null;
        invalidateSideHandler(backHandler);   backHandler = null;
        invalidateSideHandler(defaultHandler); defaultHandler = null;
    }

    // --- Capability query (sided) ---
    @Override
    public <T> LazyOptional<T> getCapability(Capability<T> cap, @Nullable Direction side) {
        if (cap == ForgeCapabilities.ITEM_HANDLER && !this.remove) {
            LazyOptional<IItemHandler> handler;
            if (side == Direction.NORTH) {
                if (frontHandler == null)
                    frontHandler = LazyOptional.of(() -> createHandler(Direction.NORTH));
                handler = frontHandler;
            } else if (side == Direction.SOUTH) {
                if (backHandler == null)
                    backHandler = LazyOptional.of(() -> createHandler(Direction.SOUTH));
                handler = backHandler;
            } else {
                if (defaultHandler == null)
                    defaultHandler = LazyOptional.of(() -> createHandler(side));
                handler = defaultHandler;
            }
            return handler.cast();
        }
        return super.getCapability(cap, side);
    }

    // --- Factory: build the correct handler for a given side ---
    private IItemHandler createHandler(Direction side) {
        // Validate: still in a level, block state still matches expectations
        if (this.getLevel() == null || this.remove) {
            return new InvWrapper(this); // safe fallback
        }
        BlockState state = this.getBlockState();
        // Example: front side exposes a limited view, back exposes full
        if (side == Direction.NORTH) {
            return new SidedInvWrapper(this, Direction.NORTH); // input-only, etc.
        }
        if (side == Direction.SOUTH) {
            return new SidedInvWrapper(this, Direction.SOUTH); // output-only, etc.
        }
        // Default: full access (mirrors BaseContainerBlockEntity pattern)
        return new InvWrapper(this);
    }

    // --- Lifecycle: full invalidation (chunk unload, BE removal) ---
    @Override
    public void invalidateCaps() {
        super.invalidateCaps();
        invalidateSideHandler(frontHandler);   frontHandler = null;
        invalidateSideHandler(backHandler);    backHandler = null;
        invalidateSideHandler(defaultHandler); defaultHandler = null;
    }

    // --- Lifecycle: revival (chunk reload, BE re-added) ---
    @Override
    public void reviveCaps() {
        super.reviveCaps();
        // Clear cache; handlers will be lazily rebuilt on next getCapability
        frontHandler = null;
        backHandler = null;
        defaultHandler = null;
    }

    // --- Helper ---
    private static void invalidateSideHandler(LazyOptional<IItemHandler> h) {
        if (h != null) h.invalidate();
    }
}",
